  "title": "Iqa‘ Bambi 8/4",
  "subtitle": "(also called Bamb)",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Bambi",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Bambi is a stretched-out Egyptian 8/4 iqa‘ that beautifully accompanies improvisations and sparse vocal sections. It is customary to start playing Bambi from the 7th beat (the dum before last), thereby emphacizing the 3 consecutive dum-s that start each cycle. An alternate form of Bambi actually starts the measure with the 3 consecutive dum-s."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Bambi 8/4 (also called Bamb ) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Bambi Iqa‘ Bambi is a stretched-out Egyptian 8/4 iqa‘ that beautifully accompanies improvisations and sparse vocal sections. It is customary to start playing Bambi from the 7 th beat (the dum before last), thereby emphacizing the 3 consecutive dum -s that start each cycle. An alternate form of Bambi actually starts the measure with the 3 consecutive dum -s. Taqasim on the Beat Simon Shaheen Turath: Masterworks of the Middle East Mawwal Ya Man Bunudak Harir Muhammad Khayri Gafnuhu ‘Allam al-Ghazal (1933) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Iqa‘ Bambi 8/4 - Form I Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan (with the last dum replaced with a tak ) Examples of the second form of Iqa‘ Bambi Andah ‘Aleik (1982) Warda Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Alf Leila w Leila (1969) Umm Kulthum Music by Baligh Hamdi (Egypt) Asamina Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Layali Lubnan (1954) Instrumental Composition Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Iqa‘ Bambi 8/4 - Form II Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
